# Massing run outputs. Every grid writes a folder of PNGs, JSON summaries and
# error logs under these paths - 6 MB and 169 files at the time this rule was
# written, all of it reproducible by re-running the command that made it. The
# corpus (inputs/) and the tools that read these folders stay tracked.
ARR/backend/tmp_mass_check/*/runs/
ARR/backend/tmp_mass_check/**/*.err
ARR/backend/runs/
ARR/backend/wire.txt

# Scratch and caches under ARR/backend. Each of these was verified by hand
# before the rule was written, and every one of them is either a log, a probe
# output or a provider cache that the code refetches:
#   *.txt at the backend root - forty ad-hoc capture files (a_aff, ax2, rk3...)
#   tmp_mass_check/<run>/      - ninety probe folders, c182 through c253
#   docs/ai-session-memory/    - 27 MB of VLM and geometry-author response cache
#   runtime/                   - 41 MB of server logs and Vworld land-use cache
# The massing corpus (tmp_mass_check/_massv2/inputs, tools) stays tracked.
ARR/backend/*.txt
!ARR/backend/requirements.txt
ARR/backend/tmp_mass_check/*/
!ARR/backend/tmp_mass_check/_massv2/
ARR/backend/tmp_mass_check/*.png
ARR/backend/tmp_mass_check/*.txt
ARR/backend/docs/ai-session-memory/
ARR/backend/docs/playwright/
ARR/backend/docs/*.log
ARR/backend/runtime/

# Root-level corpora, caches and browser profiles. Every path below was checked
# with `git ls-files <path>` and has zero tracked files, so no rule here can
# shadow something already in the repository:
#   GRL/, collected_papers/  - 136 MB and 274 MB of downloaded papers and data
#   AG-Research/data/iclr2027/arr - 513 MB of pilot run output (the manifests
#                              beside it stay visible; the private identity
#                              file is covered by AG/.gitignore)
#   .*-notebooklm-*-profile/ - Chrome and Playwright user-data directories
GRL/
collected_papers/
AG/AG-Research/data/iclr2027/arr/
.chrome-notebooklm-cdp-profile/
.playwright-notebooklm-profile/
docs/ai-session-memory/maas-cache/
/tmp_mass_check/
/tmp_mass_bench.py
/tmp_mass_diagnose.py
docs/ai-session-memory/maas-service-cache/

